    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d274">

                <pb facs="0528" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg424"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-05-23"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 23,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that a
                    statement having appeared in the newspapers to the effect that the United States
                    revenue cruisers have received orders to proceed to Behring Sea for the purpose
                    of preventing the exercise of the seal fishery by foreign vessels in
                    non-territorial waters, and that statement having been confirmed yesterday by
                    you, lam instructed by the Marquis of Salisbury to state to you that a formal
                    protest by Her Majesty’s Government against any such interference with British
                    vessels will be forwarded to you without delay.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
